WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.110
- It's Friday of we love LA
week and an honor of our season

00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:03.943
three premiere.

00:00:03.943 --> 00:00:08.128
We've been asking some LA icons
to share their LA top three.

00:00:08.128 --> 00:00:10.711
(upbeat music)

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.120
These aren't any old places
you'd find in a travel guide for

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.830
a quick search on the internet.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.950
Each top three list is a very
personal curated compilation

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.150
of the off the beaten path
spots. Not many know about.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.120
Today, we've got the voice of
LA and host of the nationalist

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.930
syndicated big boy's neighborhood,

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:35.230
which you can hear on Real 92.3 FM and LA.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.190
It's legendary radio disc jockey. Big boy.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:39.378
Get on down here.

00:00:39.378 --> 00:00:42.128
(audience claps)

00:00:45.335 --> 00:00:47.640
Hello.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.473
Yes.

00:00:50.017 --> 00:00:51.514
Hello.

00:00:51.514 --> 00:00:52.681
- How are you?

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:57.160
Congratulations.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.440
I heard that you just got
your star on the walk of fame,

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.422
right?

00:01:00.422 --> 00:01:01.379
- Yes

00:01:01.379 --> 00:01:04.500
(inaudible)

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.333
- I deserved it

00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:07.131
after 27 Years of radio.

00:01:07.131 --> 00:01:08.765
27 years of radio.

00:01:08.765 --> 00:01:10.910
I'm telling you I got
to start in Hollywood.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:13.138
I never thought that I would
get a star in Hollywood.

00:01:13.138 --> 00:01:13.971
- It's amazing.

00:01:13.971 --> 00:01:15.960
I was a kid, you know, I
grew up in Los Angeles.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.000
I would go to Hollywood.
And at one point, you know,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.111
we were homeless in our lives.

00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:22.830
I would walk from Hollywood
because I didn't have bus fare.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.240
So I would literally walk.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.078
And you would read the
stars as you're walking now.

00:01:27.078 --> 00:01:27.911
- And you're one of them now.

00:01:27.911 --> 00:01:29.866
- Now, I'm that guy.

00:01:29.866 --> 00:01:32.690
(audience claps)

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:33.730
- That's awesome

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:34.563
Kelly.

00:01:34.563 --> 00:01:37.270
I go by my star all the time
and I was just standing there

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:38.810
hoping somebody polish it,

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.950
hoping somebody would recognize me.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:41.783
- Oh, my star.

00:01:41.783 --> 00:01:43.917
- Just happen to be right here.

00:01:43.917 --> 00:01:45.200
(audience laughs)

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.210
- But wait, you love this
city. So I wanted to ask,

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:48.043
could you give us,

00:01:48.043 --> 00:01:49.660
cause I don't know this city
as well as everybody else I've

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.110
lived in Texas and Tennessee, mostly.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.840
So could you give us your
top three or you know,

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.550
places to see live music.

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.720
- Live music. There are a great spots.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.600
One spot I would say is, the
Conga room and the Conga room

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.550
is good. It's not as big,

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:05.830
but they have live great
music there. Latin fusion.

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:06.698
They have great Latin nights.

00:02:06.698 --> 00:02:07.531
- Where is this at?

00:02:07.531 --> 00:02:08.970
- This is downtown. This is downtown

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:10.070
right near the Staples Center.

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:10.903
- Okay.

00:02:10.903 --> 00:02:12.730
- Right there at the
walk. If you get a chance,

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:13.580
you should go there and their

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:14.790
Latin nights are unbelievable.

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:15.740
- What's number two?

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.601
- Number two for me, is the Greek theater.

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:18.942
- Oh, I love the Greek.

00:02:18.942 --> 00:02:19.892
- Of course.

00:02:19.892 --> 00:02:23.990
And the Greek theater is one
of those places where we have

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.925
a lot of spots out here.
That's kind of so-called

00:02:25.925 --> 00:02:29.430
under the stars, but the
Greek is just this feeling.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:33.540
It's an ambiance. It's the way
that the music sounds there.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.310
And for me personally,

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.960
that's where I saw one
of my first concerts.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.610
It was George Benson in 19.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:39.626
(cough)

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.334
(audience laughs)

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:42.167
- It was a good time.

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:43.790
- I went there, but I
went with my brother.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.180
My brother would love music.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:48.110
and he took me to this show.
And once I got into radio,

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:51.130
I was in a position where I
could take him to the Greek

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:53.520
theater, take them
backstage, meet some people.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.300
That was another place that
we had to take the bus to

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.980
and walk all the way up
the hill from Vermont.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:59.920
So, to actually drive
him and take him there,

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:00.753
amazing.

00:03:00.753 --> 00:03:02.327
- Oh my gosh, I love that.

00:03:02.327 --> 00:03:04.378
I'm actually about to
see John Legend there.

00:03:04.378 --> 00:03:05.338
(audience claps)

00:03:05.338 --> 00:03:07.671
(inaudible)

00:03:09.224 --> 00:03:11.510
- And your number one
place to see live music.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:12.343
- Number one place.

00:03:12.343 --> 00:03:14.140
There's a little spot downtown Los Angeles

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:16.300
as well, it's called the Belasco.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.133
- Belasco?

00:03:18.025 --> 00:03:20.660
- Belasco. B-E-L-A-S-C-O.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:21.493
- Okay.

00:03:21.493 --> 00:03:23.470
- And it's a spot where
it was an old theater.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:26.450
They kind of went in and
refurbished and redone the spot,

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.520
but you could see up and
coming great talent there.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.550
People that usually stopped
through Los Angeles,

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:32.730
they'll perform there as well
to get a little more intimate

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:33.804
with their crowds.

00:03:33.804 --> 00:03:34.637
- I love that.

00:03:34.637 --> 00:03:36.150
- A beautiful place downtown Los Angeles.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.140
- I love that you mentioned
like intimate places.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.534
Cause that's the coolest
thing ever. I think.

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:41.760
- I throw some birthday
parties there too, you know?

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:42.780
- Oh okay.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:43.860
- So I'm in a position where
a lot of people don't show

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:44.693
it to my birthday parties.

00:03:44.693 --> 00:03:45.767
So I got to go a little more empty.

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:48.360
(audience laughter)

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:49.840
- Well, thank you so much, Big Boy.

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:52.577
Thank you for joining us.

00:03:52.577 --> 00:03:57.236
It was an honor to have you
here, and congrats on the star.

00:03:57.236 --> 00:03:59.041
- I'll take that. Thank you guys.

00:03:59.041 --> 00:04:00.515
- Give it up for Big Boy, everybody.

00:04:00.515 --> 00:04:01.348
(audience claps)

